# cohort training runs: keep curves/GIFs/config/weights, ignore bulky artifacts.
#
# These rules use `**` rather than `*` because a `*` does not cross `/`, so every
# `runs/*/…` rule silently stopped matching the 96 runs that f80097d moved one
# level deeper into runs/archive/ (refs #44). Nothing was done wrong; the glob
# just stopped meaning what it meant, and it flipped three rules at once — 96
# ckpt_latest.pt, 79 tb/ event files and 44 host-specific .job.json got swept in.
# `**` keeps the meaning at any depth, so the next archive move is a no-op here.
runs/**/tb/
runs/*_train.log
legacy/models/
legacy/**/__pycache__/

# detached training job files (pid/host specific)
runs/**/.job.json

# ckpt_latest.pt IS the final policy — the weights every published headline is
# measured from (behavior_final.json), as against ckpt_best.pt's best-rolling-
# WINDOW snapshot. Ignoring it fleet-wide meant a fresh clone could read the
# eight baseline figures and not re-derive one of them, while the 96 superseded
# runs nobody cites carried both. That asymmetry is now the right way round: the
# live fleet in runs/ commits both checkpoints, the archive sheds the final one.
# (The 96 already tracked stay tracked — their bytes are in the pack either way,
# and untracking them would only shrink a checkout, never the history.)
runs/archive/**/ckpt_latest.pt

# generated boards + the record of what was last published to claude.ai.
# Derived from the committed behavior*.json, rewritten every time a run lands:
#   scripts/update_boards.py
runs/fleet_board.html
runs/program_board.html
runs/.boards.json
logs/
runs/*/ckpt_best_rolling.pt
# replayable episode traces (scripts/legacy_trace.py): derived, deterministic
# from (tag, scenario, seed), ~0.5 MB each. Regenerate on demand:
#   scripts/legacy_trace.py <run> [<run>...] --seed 1
runs/*/traces/
